\abstract{
% Forecasting in stock and cryptocurrency markets is challenging due to the high volatility and non-stationarity of the prices, which are influenced by unpredictable factors such as economic changes and market sentiment. Previous work in financial forecasting has shown that Echo State Networks (ESNs) can effectively model short-term stock market price movements, financial market modeling, and portfolio management by capturing complex, nonlinear patterns in highly dynamic data, making them particularly suitable for volatile environments. Despite these findings, the application of ESNs to cryptocurrency markets, especially during periods of extreme volatility, remains largely unexplored. To the best of our knowledge, this work is among the first to explore the use of ESN for cryptocurrency price forecasting. We also present a detailed chaos analysis by computing the Lyapunov exponent in highly chaotic periods. We compare our approach to existing machine learning methods and show that our approach outperforms state-of-the-art methods by a significant margin.
Forecasting stock and cryptocurrency prices is challenging due to high volatility and non-stationarity, influenced by factors like economic changes and market sentiment. Previous research shows that Echo State Networks (ESNs) can effectively model short-term stock market movements, capturing nonlinear patterns in dynamic data. To the best of our knowledge, this work is among the first to explore ESNs for cryptocurrency forecasting, especially during extreme volatility. We also conduct chaos analysis through the Lyapunov exponent in chaotic periods and show that our approach outperforms existing machine learning methods by a significant margin. Our findings are consistent with the Lyapunov exponent analysis, showing that ESNs are robust during chaotic periods and excel under high chaos compared to Boosting and  Na{\"i}ve methods.
}

\keywords{chaotic time series, cryptocurrency forecasting, echo state networks, lyapunov exponent}

