\subsection{Baseline}
The classic baseline in time series forecasting is known as the \textbf{Last Value} or simply the \textbf{Na{\"i}ve Method}. For one-step ahead forecasts, this approach uses the current price as the prediction for the next value. 
% Despite its simplicity, it has shown competitive performance, highlighting the challenges of forecasting in highly volatile and non-stationary price time series.
% Despite its simplicity, it has shown competitive performance, underscoring the challenges of forecasting due to the high volatility and non-stationarity of price time series.
