Figure~\ref{table:mannU} presents results for training windows of sizes 30 and 60, confirming the hypothesis, whereas this is not observed for window size 15. This discrepancy might be due to the short duration of these windows, posing challenges in accurately computing the Lyapunov exponent with limited points available for constructing trajectories in the embedding space.

